22],[23,27],[24,1],[24,9],[24,16],[24,21]]},"approvedInterpretations":[{"id":"interpretation-relational-refinement","text":"Prior research has connected behavioral explanations with social, relational, organizational, and enabling factors. The opportunity is more specific."}],"approvedGaps":[{"id":"gap-practical-project-support","text":"Prior construction research has applied behavioral theories to technology adoption, knowledge sharing, cooperation, and collaborative behavior, with some studies incorporating social, relational, organizational, and enabling factors. Less clear is whether access to practical support through project relationships adds explanatory value beyond established TPB predictors in explaining reported digital collaboration behavior. This study addresses that question through a network-informed extension of TPB.","display":{"lead":"Prior integration exists.","opportunity":"However, a more specific question remains.","prior":"Prior research has connected behavioral explanations with social, relational, organizational, and enabling factors.","question":"Does practical support through project relationships add explanatory value beyond established TPB predictors in explaining digital collaboration behavior?","shortQuestion":"Does practical support through project relationships add explanatory value beyond established TPB predictors for digital collaboration?","contribution":"NE-TPB examines this question by incorporating relational access to practical support into the behavioral framework.","distinction":"Here, network-informed refers to perceived access to practical support through project relationships rather than structural network measures.","from":"Behavioral intention alone","toward":"Behavior embedded within project relationships","shiftNote":"A shift in emphasis, building on prior research. Behavioral intention was not measured in this study."},"literatureExamples":[{"id":"p-368f28088b514bdd","address":[15,9],"contextNote":""},{"id":"p-5e100